node_modules/
dist/
coverage/

# The one exception. A published GitHub Action gets no `npm install` — the runner checks
# the repository out and runs `dist/main.js` as it stands — so the Action's bundle is a
# committed artifact. `node action/build.mjs --check` is the CI gate that keeps it from
# going stale, since a stale bundle keeps working while reporting an older commit's
# behaviour. Everything else under `dist/` stays ignored.
!action/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.vitest/
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Internal working notes and strategy — not part of the public open-source project.
# These record competitor analysis, decision gates and kill-signals, launch timing,
# growth targets, and how the project is built with Claude Code.
#
# What IS public: README, CONTRIBUTING, docs/rfc-0001-canonical-format.md,
# docs/determinism.md, and the per-tool precedence pages. That is what a
# contributor actually needs in order to write an adapter.
#
# The generated agent files are NOT here: CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md,
# .cursor/rules/*.mdc and .github/copilot-instructions.md are artifacts of this repo's
# own .rulegate/, rendered from public-safe rules and committed. An ignored file cannot
# be gated by `rulegate check`, so ignoring one would silently opt it out of the very
# guarantee this project sells. The hand-written working guide CLAUDE.md replaced now
# lives in the `09-working-guide` serena memory.
#
# `memory-bank/` was that store until 2026-09-09 and is now `.serena/memories/`, ignored
# by .serena/.gitignore rather than here — the entry has to sit beside the directory it
# protects, because a reader of this file would not think to look for one there.
task-breakdown.md
docs/PRD.md
docs/reserch-report.md

# Copies of files that predated rulegate, saved by `sync --force`. Local recovery
# material, not project content.
.rulegate/backup/
